pourDeriveT -- pour stage 2 (Tony ruled D1-D6, 2026-11-22; SEQ 742): rows derived from what is poured. A down="*" pour:=aRegistry
field with no row of its own gets one row a member, three cells: pourName, pourShow, pourWhat. What a member is, by value: a
value starting # a colour; a family a font; in sTYLEs with attributes a style; empty in sTYLEs a placeholder, shown as what the
look gives it; anything else its own text. A description is dESCRIPTIONs' entry of the member's name. margin=N stands the
content in, gap=N separates stacked rows, height=fit makes the top as tall as its members need, capped at 792.
PD-1  cOLOr: 14 rows; the swatches print their values, white on 3, black on 11; two descriptions (black, wall), nothing else.
PD-2  margin, gap and fit by frame: the title 12 in, 466 wide; the rows 28 apart (24 + 4); the top 452 high.
PD-3  fONTs: seven rows, each sample set in its own font; a font's row is as tall as its sample needs (titleFont 36).
PD-4  sTYLEs: emphasis is a style, its sample red; accent is a placeholder, shown as defaultLook's red swatch.
PD-5  the same form under a look of its own: accent's swatch prints the look's blue.
PD-6  a registry of mixed things: a # value a swatch, plain words their own text, an entry with no value nothing.
PD-7  cOMMANDs: 107 rows named and none read for text -- a command handed around is fired, so none is; the run goes on.
      The top is capped at 792 and rows wholly past the rows' field are noRoom: fewer than 107 names are drawn.
PD-8  a top naming height=fit with a member of no height: the cap, said by name.
PD-9  the definition is never written: no rows on it, pour still there.
